# Repair qBittorrent Search Plugins

The goal is to fix the failing search engines in qBittorrent by updating outdated plugins and replacing broken ones with a custom search backend.

## Proposed Changes

### Plugin Backups (Completed)
All existing [.py](file:///C:/Users/curtis/AppData/Local/qBittorrent/nova3/engines/dodi_repacks.py) and `.ico` files in the `engines` directory (except the working ones) have been renamed to `.old` to prevent them from causing errors and to keep a safe backup. **Note:** This is why you are currently seeing the "Search has failed" popup—the broken engines are disabled, and the new ones aren't in place yet!

### 1337x Custom Backend for Repacks
The official DODI and FitGirl sites are protected by Cloudflare/Turnstile. We will create two new plugins:
#### [NEW] dodi_repacks.py
#### [NEW] fitgirl_repacks.py
These plugins will use `1337x.to` as the search backend, strictly filtering for official uploads by "DODI" and "FitGirl" to ensure safety and reliable magnet links.

### Community Updates
We will install the latest working versions of the following plugins from active community repositories:
#### [NEW] academictorrents.py
#### [NEW] audiobookbay.py
#### [NEW] dontorrent.py
#### [NEW] esmeraldatorrent.py
#### [NEW] glotorrents.py
#### [NEW] kickasstorrents.py
#### [NEW] magnetdl.py
#### [NEW] yts.py

## Verification Plan
After writing the new [.py](file:///C:/Users/curtis/AppData/Local/qBittorrent/nova3/engines/dodi_repacks.py) files to the `engines` directory, we will manually test them using your local `python.exe` executable to ensure they scrape results correctly. Once validated, you can test them directly within the qBittorrent UI.
